[[56457,1],48][../../../../../../opal/mca/btl/openib/btl_openib_component.c:3685:handle_wc] from hpc-07 [[56457,1],56][../../../../../../opal/mca/btl/openib/btl_openib_component.c:3685:handle_wc] from hpc-07 to: unknown error polling LP CQ with status RETRY EXCEEDED ERROR status number 12 for wr_id 5c9ee9818cc0 opcode 128  vendor error 129 qp_idx 1
to: unknown error polling LP CQ with status RETRY EXCEEDED ERROR status number 12 for wr_id 5c98663f7e80 opcode 0  vendor error 129 qp_idx 1
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The InfiniBand retry count between two MPI processes has been
exceeded.  "Retry count" is defined in the InfiniBand spec 1.2
(section 12.7.38):

    The total number of times that the sender wishes the receiver to
    retry timeout, packet sequence, etc. errors before posting a
    completion error.

This error typically means that there is something awry within the
InfiniBand fabric itself.  You should note the hosts on which this
error has occurred; it has been observed that rebooting or removing a
particular host from the job can sometimes resolve this issue.

Two MCA parameters can be used to control Open MPI's behavior with
respect to the retry count:

* btl_openib_ib_retry_count - The number of times the sender will
  attempt to retry (defaulted to 7, the maximum value).
* btl_openib_ib_timeout - The local ACK timeout parameter (defaulted
  to 20).  The actual timeout value used is calculated as:

     4.096 microseconds * (2^btl_openib_ib_timeout)

  See the InfiniBand spec 1.2 (section 12.7.34) for more details.

Below is some information about the host that raised the error and the
peer to which it was connected:

  Local host:   hpc-07
  Local device: ibp176s0
  Peer host:    unknown

You may need to consult with your system administrator to get this
problem fixed.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
